msgid ""
":ref:`An ArduPilot supported board <common-autopilots>` with :ref:`GPS "
"and external compass <common-positioning-landing-page>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:13
#: 388d0b89e6284d5c8575b5529c72e9dc
msgid "RC helicopter frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:15
#: e98c3ad833b54487b8ea09b3f612d16e
msgid ""
"ArduPilot supports single rotor with conventional or direct drive tail, "
"tandem rotor, or collective pitch quad-rotor helicopter frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:18
#: f80b5763df60431aa4877a48c3fa81bc
msgid ""
"The program can be configured to fly flybar or flybarless, with CCPM "
"swash mixing or single-servo (H1) swash types. The system has flown "
"helicopters ranging from micro size with a Pixracer to large piston and "
"turbine powered machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:24
#: bd7adb742a99401cbac28afba1cabcb2
msgid "8-channel Transmitter / Receiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:26
#: ae81400fe89446b9aafda491fce7b8d7
msgid ""
"Your transmitter & receiver must support minimum 8 channels (elevator, "
"aileron, collective pitch, rudder, flight mode, tuning knob, auxiliary "
"function switch, throttle hold)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:31
#: fce2008cfe5840e781eeb40b25590b88
msgid "Use of electric and engine governors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:33
#: a2c003297d2f4b3599ad699dfbd4fc24
msgid ""
"If you intend to use any Copter flight control modes other than Acro and "
"Stabilize, it is recommended that the speed controller you purchase for "
"an electric helicopter have a governor mode. For piston and turbine "
"engines a governor is required. This is because Copter will be "
"controlling the pitch of the main blades automatically along with its "
"internal throttle control system. The throttle curve in ArduPilot will be"
" used for fallback and feedforward for piston and turbine engines in the "
"event the governor fails in flight, and for faster governor response on "
"high collective pitch loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:42
#: b1f1cc16c7294d4992c9e05a865561f7
msgid ""
"For electric helicopters ArduPilot will set the throttle for the ESC "
"governor to hold the headspeed constant at all times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:46
#: 5d45f1d6fefd4e4fa62bb9e5a46f3ab7
msgid "Digital servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:48
#: db4ce545782242e994f181ac826d5f17
msgid ""
"You should use digital servos instead of analog. Digital servos have much"
" faster response time, more accurate positioning, and your helicopter "
"will fly much more accurate and stable with digital servos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:53
#: 6cd5127f2c904233af2915c54ff6c8a2
msgid "Batteries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:55
#: 1ffc2cf8e5d148089d37c3952b6ab0cf
msgid ""
"There are no special requirements for flight batteries. However, as a "
"general rule, it is safer if you can have a separate motor battery and "
"radio battery on electric helicopters. Electric motor power systems can "
"have very high power draw in helicopters. Having separate batteries will "
"prevent \"brownout\" of power to the flight electronics."
msgstr ""

